    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='SQL Injection with Hibernate and PostgreSQL',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains S Q L Injection with Hibernate, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] An object-relational mapper is not a shield. A J P Q L or native query built by pasting text into it is injectable, J P Q L can reach every entity and not just the one it names, and the fix is the same as ever: bind parameters, choose sort keys from a list, and connect as a database user who can only do what the page needs. [[slnc 600]] Think of it this way. [[slnc 300]] A librarian who fetches books for you. If the slip you hand over is copied word for word into the librarian\'s own instruction sheet, a slip that says "this book, and also the staff files" is followed. If the slip is only ever read as a title, it cannot give orders. And a librarian who has no key to the staff room cannot fetch from it even when fooled. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online store\'s product search. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will be able to: [[slnc 300]] Explain why J P Q L and native queries built from strings are injectable. [[slnc 300]] Show how J P Q L can read entities that the query does not name. [[slnc 300]] Fix a query with named parameters, Criteria or an allow-list.'),
